{
  "_notes": "Hand-verified golden set for D4.png. Ids/coordinates from the pipeline's own detections, TYPE corrected by visual inspection. CONNECTIONS hand-traced from the schematic 2026-08-30, net by net. Key structural fact: IC1 is an optocoupler, so the input side (S1, R1, IC1 pins 1/2, BATT-13V) is galvanically isolated from the output side -- the bottom rail is TWO separate segments (verified at the pin 2 / pin 4 junction, there is a visible gap), so BATT-13V shares a node only with IC1, not with the 224V side. Nets: N_SW(BATT-13V+ - S1 - R1: S1's other side goes to the +13V battery terminal), N_LED(R1-IC1 pin1), N_GND_IN(BATT-13V - / IC1 pin2), N_GND_OUT(IC1 pin4, T1 emitter, T3, T4 source, BATT-224V -), N_T1B(R3-T1 base-IC1 pin5), N_T1C(R2-T1 collector-R4 left), N_T2B(R4 right-T2 base), N_TOP(+V rail before R6: R2/R3 top, T2 collector, C1+, ZD1 top, R6 left), N_TOP_B(after R6: LOAD top, D1 cathode, BATT-224V+), N_OUT(T2/T3 emitters-R5 left), N_GATE(R5 right, C1-, ZD1 bottom, T4 gate), N_DRAIN(LOAD bottom, D1 anode, T4 drain). Confidence ~85%: the T1/R4 and R5/gate routing are dense and a couple of terminal assignments are judgement calls. ZD1 and D1 are pipeline misses, kept with estimated coordinates as false negatives; connectivity is scored only over pairs whose both endpoints were detected, so ZD1/D1 pairs are skipped, not penalised. SYM_015 (a duplicate box on IC1) is intentionally omitted.",
